WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:07.799
Hi! It's Michelle from Lab Muffin Beauty
Science here, chemistry PhD and fan of

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:11.370
research-based skincare. Today I'm going
to be talking about the science behind

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:16.830
two very popular Neutrogena products:
the Ultra Gentle Daily Cleanser, and the

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.060
Clear Pore Cleanser and Mask. I think
there's this idea that picking the right

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:26.880
cleanser is just about low PH, and these
two are low pH, but there's a lot more to

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.260
cleanser formulations than just that.
This video is sponsored by Neutrogena,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.280
and I'm super grateful that they think
my content is worth supporting. If you

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.850
like nerding out about the science behind
beauty products, make sure you subscribe,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:49.140
and click the notification bell so don't
miss any videos. Neutrogena Ultra Gentle

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.989
Daily Cleanser is one of my new favorite
drugstore cleansers.

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:55.620
It's a foaming cleanser, which is my
favorite type because it spreads over

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:00.420
skin nicely and washes off easily I know
this is common perception that foaming

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:04.739
cleansers are harsh and stripping, and
this comes from the fact that for a long

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.030
time the only ingredient that would foam
really well was sodium lauryl sulfate.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:13.110
This ingredient is usually a bit on the
harsher side, unless it's formulated

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.460
very carefully. But in the last few
decades chemists have realized that you

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.229
can blend together gentler ingredients
and still get a really nice foam. So this

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:25.880
cleanser, even though it foams really
well, doesn't contain harsh surfactants.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.119
Surfactants are the cleaning ingredients
in cleansers. This cleanser uses

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.020
hydrophobically modified polymer technology
which was developed by scientists at

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.290
Neutrogena. Generally the harshest
ingredients in the cleanser are the

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.340
surfactants. Basically this cleanser has
ingredients that act like a little

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.149
reservoir for the surfactants, so they're
all clean together into one big mass

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:48.570
When it's clumped together the
surfactants actually foam better in the

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.340
cleanser. The clump is also too big to
get into skin and irritate it, and that

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.969
means that it's actually gentler and
less irritating than some non-foaming

00:01:56.969 --> 00:02:01.170
cleansers. But the surfactant molecules
can still detach one by one from this

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:05.159
clump, and so it still acts as an
effective cleanser that gets rid of dirt

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:09.179
and grease on your skin. So this doesn't
have that harshness or stripping that

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:12.000
you might expect from a cleanser that
foams up and cleans

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.530
skin effectively. This also has a ton of
my favorite humectant ingredient:

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.310
glycerine. Glycerine is really good at
holding on to water, so it acts like a

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:24.210
little sponge that sits on your skin and
keeps it hydrated. This is particularly

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:28.350
important in a cleanser, because
cleansing is generally the harshest step

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:32.250
in a skincare routine. Wet skin is also
more permeable, which means that during

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.180
and after you cleanse that's when your
skin is most prone to dehydrating and

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.950
glycerin helps counteract this effect.
This cleanser is lightly fragranced.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.640
The fragrance is hypoallergenic and it
doesn't contain any known allergens or

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.600
essential oils. I really like how this
cleanser doesn't strip my skin and it

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.739
leaves my skin feeling soft and smooth.
My skin gets dehydrator really easily,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:56.760
especially right after I wash it, so it's
really good to have a drugstore cleanser

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.780
that keeps my skin hydrated and happy. It
also comes in a pump which is my

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:10.500
favorite type of packaging. It makes it
super convenient to use.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.010
The other product I'm talking about in this video
is the Clear Pool Cleanser or a mask.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:17.459
This is a product that's designed to
help with short contact therapy with

00:03:17.459 --> 00:03:22.350
benzoyl peroxide. It has 3.5% benzoyl
peroxide. You can use this either as a

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:26.100
regular cleanser, or you can put it on as
a mask that you wash off after about

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:30.150
five minutes. Benzoyl peroxide is a
classic acne treatment and it's so

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.260
effective that it's usually regulated as
a drug in most countries. It's been used

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.730
for acne since the 1930s and it works in
a few different ways. I think most people

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.829
know that it's antibacterial and acts
to kill the bacteria formerly known as

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:49.500
Propionibacterium acnes, now called QT
bacterium acnes. These bacteria are one

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:53.730
of the four contributing factors to acne
and it kills them in a way that doesn't

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.200
cause bacterial resistance. It also acts
on two more contributors to acne;

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.220
It prevents clogged pores, and it reduces
inflammation. A lot of people are

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:07.500
sensitive to benzoyl peroxide. It causes
irritation in up to 40% of people who

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.540
use it. You might get redness, dryness,
peeling, and stinging. Luckily it looks like

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.709
wash-off products with benzoyl peroxide
work pretty well at treating acne and it

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:20.609
does it with less irritation. It works in
a really short amount of time so you

00:04:20.609 --> 00:04:22.650
don't have to leave it on your skin and
have it irritate.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:26.820
There's also the bleaching
issue benzoyl peroxide can break up dye

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:31.380
molecules and fabrics so it can bleach
patches on your clothes, pillowcases, and

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.759
towels. This product washes off, so it's a
lot less likely to happen, and it's

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:39.449
particularly good for treating acne on
your body because it's really hard to

00:04:39.449 --> 00:04:43.410
avoid getting that on your clothes.
This also has glycerin as the second

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:46.889
ingredient on the ingredients list and
that's really useful because it can

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:51.360
counteract the drying effect of benzoyl
peroxide. Most people will probably need

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.260
to use a moisturizer afterwards anyway
because benzoyl peroxide is quite harsh,

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.900
and of course you need to wear a
sunscreen as well.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.340
There's also Kaolin and bentonite clay
which helps soak up oils, which deals

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.479
with the fourth contributor to acne,
which is excess oil production. It's

00:05:06.479 --> 00:05:11.250
actually the only clay mask that
actively kills bacteria as well. I love

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.570
how easily the spreads on my skin and
washes off my skin is oily and acne

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:19.710
prone, but sometimes I find benzoyl
peroxide still a bit too harsh because

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.300
I'm also quite prone to dehydration and
my skin is sometimes a bit dry from

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:28.260
using retinoids. If I want to use benzoyl
peroxide without having an extra layer

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.090
on my skin, or that extra irritation, this
is great. I usually put it on before I go

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:36.750
into the shower or even in the shower
and then wash my hair and then wash it

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.020
off. This cleanser does have menthol in
it which gives it that tingling or

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:44.580
cooling effect, and it's probably my only
complaint about this product, especially

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:48.210
because I'm in Australia and we're
heading into winter and I am cold enough.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:51.630
I do know that a lot of people like that
refreshing feeling in their acne

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:56.130
products. It's not bad for you, it's just
a personal preference and it is actually

00:05:56.130 --> 00:06:00.060
quite useful to tell if you've washed it
off properly before you go and blot your

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.599
face and get benzoyl peroxide everywhere.
So that's my breakdown of those -

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:07.139
Neutrogena products: the Ultra Gentle
Daily Cleanser and the Clear Pool

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:10.770
Cleanser Mask. I hope you found this
video interesting. Let me know what you

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.289
thought of these products if you've
tried them before. Thanks again to

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:16.800
Neutrogena for partnering with me. If you
like videos on the science behind beauty

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.130
products, you can click the thumbs up and
